From 80d4591ed64a93a393e3987e44ba02a04d2c7041 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:06:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Release the active_pr guard on portable review
 evidence; add operator kanban resume

A card that parks on an exact-head review (dependency_wait with an authenticated
review_checkpoint) could stay respawn-guarded forever after the review finished on
another gateway: the review card was foreign to the importing file (only in the
Board replica), and the move-scoped parent-evidence mirror required a checkpointed
queued move, which capacity/drain moves never carry.

- kanban_move_parent_evidence: also mirror a foreign parent's result when the
  child's own latest run parked with an authenticated review checkpoint matched by
  portable run uid (never integer ids). prepare() is scoped to children of foreign
  parents; local parents' rows still always decide.
- kanban resume <id> --reason: operator-only supported handoff for a READY card held
  active_pr. Refused under worker lineage (HERMES_KANBAN_TASK / WORKER_TASK /
  delegated child); records operator_resumed + RESUMED: comment; one continuation
  of the named latest run (lapses once a newer run is claimed); never a merge.
- active_pr_reason: handoff checks extracted to _handed_off_after (CC).

Cases: t_01a1cde626be2ada, t_01a1c59e0410b2fb, t_01a1cda0a1585230.
